// THE BOOK OF THE HEAVENLY COW ("The Destruction of Mankind"), in Budge's
// English from Legends of the Gods (1912), section by section.
//
// The text comes from heavenly-cow-text.ts, generated by
// scripts/texts/budge-heavenly-cow.py from the Project Gutenberg e-text
// compared word by word with OCRs of two printed copies. Budge prints the book
// in five sections, the first without a numeral and the others numbered II–V;
// those five are the units. The two long sections (I and V) hold no text of
// their own: beneath them, the archive's own parts, cut at a change of scene.
// Budge's hieroglyphic text, transliteration and footnotes are left out.
// Hornung's edition and Lichtheim's English are in copyright and are cited,
// never quoted.
//
// Nothing is marked verified, and Budge's five sections have not been checked
// against Hornung's division (inventoryVerified stays false).

